---
import fixtures from '../../public/aegis-data/meeting.json';
import { methodLabel, pathLabel } from '../lib/meeting-view';
const initial = fixtures.runs['design:baseline'];
---
<div class="meeting-lab" data-meeting-lab>
  <section class="ag-section ml-section" id="meeting-lab" aria-labelledby="meeting-heading">
    <span id="execution" class="ml-anchor"></span>
    <div class="ml-heading"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">TRY IT / A MEETING YOU CAN FOLLOW</p><h2 id="meeting-heading">Meeting notes in.<br />Clear next steps out.</h2></div><span class="ml-status" data-m-connection>Recorded learning example</span></div>
    <p class="ml-intro">Read a short fictional meeting, choose the conditions, and create a recap. Then select any output to see <strong>exactly where it came from</strong>.</p>
    <details class="ml-lessons" open><summary>Six small experiments to learn by doing</summary><div class="ml-lesson-grid">{fixtures.experiments.map(item=><button type="button" data-m-experiment={item.id} aria-pressed={item.id==='baseline'?'true':'false'}>{item.title}</button>)}</div><p data-m-goal>{fixtures.experiments[0].goal}</p></details>
    <div class="ml-toolbar"><div><label for="meeting-mode">How should this demo run?</label><select id="meeting-mode" data-m-mode disabled><option value="learning">Learning mode · no AI required</option><option value="model" disabled>Real AI model · not configured</option></select></div><div class="ml-method-note" data-m-mode-help>Python runs text extraction, policy checks and the queue. Device conditions and local/cloud model profiles are simulated. Learning mode never sends your notes to a model.</div><button type="button" class="ag-button ag-button--primary" data-m-run disabled>Create summary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
    <p class="ml-message" role="status" data-m-message>Start with the example below, or try one of the lessons.</p>
    <p class="ml-stale" data-m-stale hidden>Inputs changed. The output still belongs to the previous run. Create a new summary to update it.</p>
    <div class="ml-workspace">
      <div class="ml-input ml-card">
        <div class="ml-card-title"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">1 / INPUT</p><h3>The meeting notes</h3></div><button type="button" class="ml-text-button" data-m-edit>Edit notes</button></div>
        <div class="ml-samples" role="group" aria-label="Meeting examples">{fixtures.samples.map(sample=><button type="button" data-m-sample={sample.id} aria-pressed={sample.id==='design'?'true':'false'}>{sample.title}</button>)}</div>
        <div data-m-editor hidden><label for="meeting-notes">Use fictional notes. One contribution per line, with a speaker name.</label><textarea id="meeting-notes" data-m-notes rows="7" maxlength="6000" spellcheck="false" disabled>{fixtures.samples[0].notes}</textarea><p class="ml-small">The learning extractor recognizes explicit “I’ll…” or “I will…” commitments. It leaves unstated owners or deadlines blank.</p></div>
        <div data-m-source-view><p class="ml-small" data-m-source-label>Notes used for the displayed result. Select a line to find its outputs.</p><div class="ml-sources" data-m-sources>{initial.sentences.map(sentence=><button type="button" data-source-id={sentence.id} aria-pressed="false"><span class="ml-source-number">{sentence.id.replace('s','')}</span><span><strong>{sentence.speaker}</strong><span>{sentence.text}</span></span></button>)}</div></div>
        <div class="ml-conditions"><h4>What is allowed?</h4><label class="ml-switch"><input type="checkbox" data-m-private checked disabled /><span><strong>Keep notes on this device</strong><small>On: cloud processing is forbidden. Off: you permit cloud processing.</small></span></label><label class="ml-switch"><input type="checkbox" data-m-offline disabled /><span><strong>Network offline</strong><small>Cloud candidates cannot run without a connection.</small></span></label><label class="ml-switch"><input type="checkbox" data-m-local checked disabled /><span><strong>Local backend available</strong><small>In learning mode, this changes a fictional model profile.</small></span></label>
          <details class="ml-advanced"><summary>More conditions and failure tests</summary><label class="ml-switch"><input type="checkbox" data-m-busy disabled /><span>Busy device · simulated CPU/memory pressure</span></label><label class="ml-switch"><input type="checkbox" data-m-cloud checked disabled /><span>Cloud candidate available</span></label><label for="meeting-failure">Test a provider failure</label><select id="meeting-failure" data-m-failure disabled><option value="none">No failure</option><option value="timeout">First provider times out</option><option value="invalid_output">First provider cites invented evidence</option></select></details>
        </div>
        <div class="ml-plan"><span class="ag-eyebrow">CURRENT PLAN / SELECTED CONDITIONS</span><h4 data-m-plan-title>{pathLabel(initial.plan.placement.selected)}</h4><p data-m-plan-reason>{initial.plan.placement.rationale}</p><p class="ml-small" data-m-plan-privacy>{initial.plan.privacy}</p><details><summary>Why were other paths rejected?</summary><div data-m-rejected>{Object.entries(initial.plan.policy.rejected).map(([key,reasons])=><p><strong>{pathLabel(key)}</strong><br />{reasons.join(' · ')}</p>)}</div></details></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ml-output ml-card" id="meeting-output">
        <div class="ml-card-title"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">2 / OUTPUT</p><h3 data-m-result-heading>Your meeting recap</h3></div><span class="ml-output-count" data-m-count>{initial.document?.actions.length} actions</span></div>
        <p class="ml-result-source" data-m-result-source>Recorded Python example · {methodLabel(initial)}</p><p class="ml-small" data-m-path>Used: {pathLabel(initial.actual_backend)}</p>
        <div class="ml-outcome-notice" data-m-outcome hidden></div>
        <div data-m-document>
          <section class="ml-result-section"><h4>Key points</h4><p class="ml-small" data-m-summary-hint>Learning mode selects source excerpts. It does not generate an AI-written summary.</p><div data-m-summary>{initial.document?.summary.map(item=><button type="button" class="ml-evidence-item" data-item-sources={item.source_ids.join(' ')}><span>{item.text}</span><small>Source {item.source_ids.map(id=>id.replace('s','')).join(', ')} ↖</small></button>)}</div></section>
          <section class="ml-result-section"><h4>Who does what?</h4><div data-m-actions>{initial.document?.actions.map(item=><article class="ml-action"><button type="button" class="ml-evidence-item" data-item-sources={item.source_ids.join(' ')}><span>{item.text}</span><small>Check source {item.source_ids.map(id=>id.replace('s','')).join(', ')} ↖</small></button><dl><div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>{item.owner||'Not stated'}</dd></div><div><dt>Due</dt><dd>{item.due||'Not stated'}</dd></div></dl></article>)}</div></section>
          <section class="ml-result-section"><h4>What was decided?</h4><div data-m-decisions>{initial.document?.decisions.map(item=><button type="button" class="ml-evidence-item" data-item-sources={item.source_ids.join(' ')}><span>{item.text}</span><small>Source {item.source_ids.map(id=>id.replace('s','')).join(', ')} ↖</small></button>)}</div></section>
        </div>
        <aside class="ml-evidence-note" aria-live="polite"><span class="ag-eyebrow">WHY IS THIS HERE?</span><p data-m-evidence>Select a key point, action, decision, or source line. The matching evidence will appear here and light up in the notes.</p></aside>
        <p class="ml-small">Review the result before using it. No external task, email or notification is created.</p>
        <div class="ml-result-tools"><button type="button" class="ml-text-button" data-m-pin>Save for comparison</button><button type="button" class="ml-text-button" data-m-download>Download recap ↓</button></div><div class="ml-comparison" data-m-comparison hidden></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="ml-queue ml-card" aria-labelledby="queue-heading"><div class="ml-card-title"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">THE SCHEDULER / WHAT RUNS FIRST?</p><h3 id="queue-heading">A meeting request can take priority.</h3></div><span class="ml-status" data-m-queue-mode>One Python worker</span></div><p class="ml-small">Add a small reference-indexing task, then create your summary. Work yields between chunks. Tasks advance only when you run or step; this demo does not create continuous device load.</p><div class="ml-queue-controls"><button type="button" class="ag-button" data-m-background disabled>Add reference indexing</button><button type="button" class="ag-button" data-m-step disabled>Run next work turn →</button><label class="ml-inline-check"><input type="checkbox" data-m-manual disabled /> Study the queue one turn at a time</label><button type="button" class="ml-text-button" data-m-cancel hidden>Cancel queued summary</button></div><div class="ml-queue-items" data-m-queue-items><p class="ml-empty">No pending work. Add reference indexing to try the priority experiment.</p></div><details class="ml-advanced" data-m-history-panel hidden><summary>Earlier completed work</summary><div data-m-queue-history></div></details><p class="ml-small" data-m-indexed></p><ol class="ml-queue-events" data-m-queue-events></ol></section>
    <details class="ml-trace" open><summary>Study this run, one decision at a time</summary><div class="ml-trace-layout"><div class="ml-phase-list" role="group" aria-label="Completed execution steps" data-m-phases>{initial.trace.map((step,index)=><button type="button" data-m-phase={index} aria-pressed={index===0?'true':'false'}>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')} · {step.title}</button>)}</div><div class="ml-phase-detail"><p class="ag-eyebrow" data-m-phase-label>STEP 1 / COMPLETED EVIDENCE</p><h3 data-m-phase-title>{initial.trace[0].title}</h3><p data-m-phase-explanation>{initial.trace[0].explanation}</p><p class="ml-small" data-m-phase-timing>Snapshot · no separate timing claimed</p><details><summary>Technical payload</summary><pre data-m-phase-payload>{JSON.stringify(initial.trace[0].data,null,2)}</pre></details></div></div><details><summary>Full result and trace JSON</summary><pre data-m-json>{JSON.stringify(initial,null,2)}</pre></details></details>
  </section>
  <section class="ag-section ml-section" id="runtime-model" aria-labelledby="runtime-model-heading"><p class="ag-eyebrow">FOUR RESPONSIBILITIES / PLAIN ENGLISH</p><h2 id="runtime-model-heading">Observe. Check.<br />Choose. Run.</h2><p class="ml-intro">Select a role to connect the architecture to something you just tried.</p><div class="ml-roles" role="group" aria-label="Runtime roles"><button type="button" data-m-role="telemetry" aria-pressed="true"><span>1 / What is happening?</span><strong>Telemetry</strong></button><button type="button" data-m-role="policy" aria-pressed="false"><span>2 / What is allowed?</span><strong>Policy engine</strong></button><button type="button" data-m-role="scheduler" aria-pressed="false"><span>3 / Where and when?</span><strong>Scheduler</strong></button><button type="button" data-m-role="execution" aria-pressed="false"><span>4 / Who does the work?</span><strong>Execution backend</strong></button></div><div class="ml-role-detail"><p class="ag-eyebrow" data-m-role-context>CURRENT SELECTED CONDITIONS</p><h3 data-m-role-title>Telemetry observes conditions.</h3><p data-m-role-explanation>Device/network inputs tell the runtime what resources are available. These inputs are simulated here; Python execution time is actually measured.</p><p class="ml-role-example" data-m-role-example></p></div><p class="ml-small">Outcomes return to the trace for inspection. Automatic policy tuning, hardware counters and an adaptive feedback controller remain future work.</p></section>
</div>
<script>
  import { initMeetingLab } from '../scripts/meeting';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-meeting-lab]');
  if(root) void initMeetingLab(root);
</script>
